    green_count: 2-4
    red_count: 1-4
    total_count: 4-6 (must fit in 6 slots)
    length: 2-8 cells each
    placement: bars do not touch grid border rows (first/last row all bg) [observed]
    overlap: bars on same row allowed if different colors and non-overlapping columns
    bg_fraction: ~85-87% of grid is background [observed]
  output:
    shape: fixed 2x3
    fill: green cells first then red cells in row-major order, remaining slots black
    each colored cell represents one bar of that color (count, not position/length)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (simple counting task, no inversion needed)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims R in [10,15], C in [10,19]
    2. Pick background color from {blue, gray, azure, maroon, orange, yellow, pink} (not green/red/black)
    3. Fill grid with background
    4. Pick green_count in [2,4], red_count in [1,4] with total in [4,6]
    5. For each bar, pick a row (avoiding row 0 and row R-1), a start column, and length in [2, min(8, C-start)]
    6. Place bars ensuring no cell overlap; bars of different colors may share a row if columns do not overlap
    7. Verify exactly green and red foreground colors, bg is most frequent color
